.TH "BASH\-SERVER\-CLIENT\-CSHARP" "7" "2026\-02\-01" "bash\-server 0.1.0" "bash\-server concepts"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The C# client binding provides a \f[CR]Task\f[R]\-based async/await
interface to the bash\-server v2 NDJSON protocol.
It is implemented as the \f[CR]BashServer.Client\f[R] NuGet package,
targets .NET 6.0 or later, and depends only on the .NET standard library
(\f[CR]System.Net.Sockets\f[R], \f[CR]System.IO.Pipes\f[R],
\f[CR]System.Text.Json\f[R]).
.PP
The binding uses a background \f[CR]Task\f[R] that reads NDJSON lines
from the transport and dispatches them to per\-channel
\f[CR]TaskCompletionSource\f[R] instances and registered event handlers.
All request/response operations are async and accept a
\f[CR]CancellationToken\f[R] for cancellation and timeout control.
.SH CONCEPTS
.SH Installation
The package is located at \f[CR]bash\-server/clients/csharp/\f[R] and
uses the .NET CLI:
.IP
.EX
cd bash\-server/clients/csharp
dotnet build
.EE
.PP
To run tests:
.IP
.EX
dotnet test
.EE
.PP
To create a NuGet package:
.IP
.EX
dotnet pack
.EE
.SH NuGet package
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]PackageReference\f[R] Include=\(dqBashServer.Client\(dq Version=\(dq0.1.0\(dq />
.EE
.PP
Or via the CLI:
.IP
.EX
dotnet add package BashServer.Client
.EE
