Properties are PascalCase (C# convention).
JSON serialization uses \f[CR]System.Text.Json\f[R] with
\f[CR]JsonPropertyName\f[R] attributes to map to the
\f[CR]snake_case\f[R] wire\-format names:
.IP
.EX
\f[B]public\f[R] record EvalResult(
    [property: JsonPropertyName(\(dqstdout\(dq)] string Stdout,
    [property: JsonPropertyName(\(dqstderr\(dq)] string Stderr,
    [property: JsonPropertyName(\(dqexit_code\(dq)] int ExitCode
);
.EE
.SH Error handling
All errors derive from \f[CR]BashClientException\f[R], which extends
\f[CR]Exception\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
BashClientException
    AuthException          \-\- Authentication failed
    ProtocolException      \-\- Malformed frame or message
    TimeoutException       \-\- Operation timed out / cancelled
    TransportException     \-\- Socket or I/O error
    ServerException        \-\- Server returned error response
        .Channel           \-\- Channel that produced the error
.EE
.PP
Standard \f[CR]try\f[R]/\f[CR]catch\f[R] patterns:
.IP
.EX
\f[B]try\f[R]
{
    await client.AuthAsync(wrongToken);
}
\f[B]catch\f[R] (AuthException)
{
    Console.Error.WriteLine(\(dqbad token\(dq);
}

\f[B]using\f[R] var cts = \f[B]new\f[R] CancellationTokenSource(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));
\f[B]try\f[R]
{
    var result = await client.EvalAsync(\(dqsleep 60\(dq, cts.Token);
}
\f[B]catch\f[R] (TimeoutException)
{
    Console.Error.WriteLine(\(dqcommand timed out\(dq);
}
\f[B]catch\f[R] (OperationCanceledException)
{
    Console.Error.WriteLine(\(dqoperation was cancelled\(dq);
}

\f[B]try\f[R]
{
    await client.State.GetVarAsync(\(dqNONEXISTENT\(dq);
}
\f[B]catch\f[R] (ServerException ex)
{
    Console.Error.WriteLine($\(dqserver error on channel {ex.Channel}\(dq);
}
.EE
.PP
\f[CR]TimeoutException\f[R] is thrown when a
\f[CR]CancellationToken\f[R] expires.
\f[CR]OperationCanceledException\f[R] is thrown when the caller
explicitly cancels the token.
Both can be caught together if the distinction is not needed.
